### ENGINE 6 — The Doctor (Decision Engine)

**Does NOT measure. Does NOT draw.**  
It only **decides which single mistake to fix first**, using motor learning principles.

This is the most important engine. A naive system would say "fix the wrist (score: 0.20)." A smart system says "fix the pelvis first (score: 0.50), because fixing the pelvis will automatically improve the wrist."

**Three layers of logic — applied in order:**

#### Layer 1 — Bandwidth Gate (Ignore Trivial Errors)
```
Research: Bandwidth feedback (Schmidt, 1991 — Sports Science)
Ignore errors that are small enough to not matter.

BANDWIDTH = 0.12  (normalized units)

If JointError.distance < 0.12 → SILENT. Don't distract the user.
If JointError.distance ≥ 0.12 → Candidate for correction.
```

#### Layer 2 — Motor Learning Priority (Kinematic Sort)
```
Research: Proximal-to-distal motor learning principle.
Always fix the CORE before the EXTREMITIES.

Utility Score = (1.0 - boneScore) × kineticWeight

  Core bones   (weight 0.5): spine, pelvis, shoulders
  Primary bones (weight 0.3): upper arms, thighs
  Secondary bones (weight 0.2): forearms, calves, wrists

Example:
  left_wrist:   score=0.20, weight=0.2 → Utility = 0.80 × 0.2 = 0.160
  pelvis:       score=0.50, weight=0.5 → Utility = 0.50 × 0.5 = 0.250

Winner: PELVIS (despite left_wrist having a worse raw score)
```

#### Layer 3 — FSM Hysteresis (No Flickering)
```
Research: Finite State Machine with hysteresis thresholds.
Once a bottleneck is chosen, HOLD it until it is truly fixed.

PROMOTE_THRESHOLD = 0.60  (bone must be THIS bad to become bottleneck)
DEMOTE_THRESHOLD  = 0.82  (bottleneck is only released when THIS good)

State:
  If currentBottleneck == null:
    → Find highest Utility Score bone
    → Set as bottleneck

  If currentBottleneck != null:
    If currentBottleneck.score > 0.82:
      → Release it. Find next bottleneck.
    Else:
      → HOLD. Keep showing the same instruction. Do NOT switch.
```

**Why hysteresis?** Without it, the arrow would jump between joints every frame as ML Kit fluctuates. With it, the instruction stays stable long enough for the user to actually react.

**Engine 6 Output — `GuidanceSignal`:**
```dart
class GuidanceSignal {
  final String bottleneckBoneName;         // "left_humerus"
  final PoseLandmarkType bottleneckJoint;  // leftElbow (the distal joint)
  final double correctionDx;              // normalized direction to move
  final double correctionDy;
  final double errorMagnitude;            // how far off (normalized)
  final CorrectionDirection direction;    // UP / DOWN / LEFT / RIGHT / etc.
  final bool isPostureAcceptable;         // score >= 0.85 → hide all guidance
}

enum CorrectionDirection {
  up, down, left, right,
  upLeft, upRight, downLeft, downRight
}

// Direction calculation:
final angle = math.atan2(dy, dx) * 180 / math.pi;
// -45° to  45°  → RIGHT
//  45° to 135°  → DOWN
// -135° to -45° → UP
// outside above → LEFT / diagonals
```

